infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title ThreadPoolExecutor vs ProcessPoolExecutor
  desc One interface, two physics — shared memory and the GIL vs true parallelism and the pickle tax
  compares
    - label ThreadPoolExecutor: shared memory, I/O-bound
      children
        - label Submit in microseconds
          desc A 500 MB DataFrame passes by reference — no copy
        - label Wins on I/O-bound work
          desc HTTP, DB, S3 block in the kernel where the GIL is released
        - label The GIL never stops races
          desc += is 3 bytecodes; check-then-act still needs a Lock
    - label ProcessPoolExecutor: true parallelism, pickle tax
      children
        - label Real CPU parallelism
          desc Separate interpreters; pure-Python compute overlaps for real
        - label Pickle tax both ways
          desc ~1 s per 100 MB each direction — ship paths and IDs, not data
        - label fork copies locks, not their owners
          desc Set mp_context=spawn; never trust the platform default
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
